        <h2>How We Pick the Under-$20 Wall</h2>
        <p>We taste a lot of samples, and the bar for this shelf is simple: would we bring it to a friend's house? Vintages change, importers change, and a wine that was a steal two years ago can quietly drift. So the list rotates. If you want to know what's drinking best right now, ask at <a href="/east-austin.html">East Austin</a> or <a href="/lakeway.html">Lakeway</a>, or check our <a href="/faq.html">FAQ</a> for how special orders work. Craving a cocktail instead? Our <a href="/guides/classic-cocktails-at-home.html">classic cocktails guide</a> has you covered.</p>

        <h2>Common Questions</h2>
        <h3>What is the best red wine under $20?</h3>
        <p>For value, Spanish Garnacha and Côtes du Rhône are hard to beat. Both deliver ripe fruit, spice, and food-friendliness that usually costs more elsewhere.</p>
        <h3>Is there good Texas wine under $20?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Fall Creek, Becker's Iconoclast line, and Llano Estacado all make reliable bottles under $20, with Tempranillo and Viognier as standout Texas grapes.</p>
        <h3>What sparkling wine is closest to Champagne for the money?</h3>
        <p>French Crémant. It's made by the same traditional method as Champagne, just from other regions of France, and many bottles come in under $20.</p>
